  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Revival After the Great War (2021), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 4 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 3,477 times and is discussed on Wikipedia.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Revival After the Great War by Luc Verpoest, Leen Engelen, Rajesh Heynickx and others was published by Leuven University Press in 2021. Conceptually, the work connects to Politics, Scope (computer science), Political science, Spanish Civil War and World War II.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 4 citations. Citations peaked in 2025 with 2 citing works. Notable citing venues include Historische Zeitschrift, Lecture notes in civil engineering and Architecture_MPS. The citing works include 2 journal articles and 1 book chapter. They come from 2 countries, led by Belgium and Ukraine.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It is discussed on Wikipedia (2 mentions). It has been downloaded 3,477 times via OAPEN. A further 2 mentions appear in other attention signals. Its subject matter aligns with Sustainable cities and communities among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven.</p>",
